    <name>U6 PRETEST</name>
    <intro>&lt;h3&gt;Unit 1 Pretest — Diagnostic Readiness Check&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Answer 10 questions independently before beginning the unit lesson. One attempt is available. Submit your complete attempt to see your score and right/wrong indicators.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No course-grade weight:&lt;/strong&gt; This pretest counts 0% toward your course grade. Completion requires a submitted, graded attempt—not a passing score. Use the result to identify what you need to learn; a low diagnostic score does not trigger a mastery intervention.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accelerated-path consideration:&lt;/strong&gt; A score of 90% or above makes you eligible for consideration for this unit only. A parent or guidance request is also required; placement is not automatic. If approved, you still complete Notebook Evidence, Checkpoint, lesson quizzes, and the unit assessment. For notebook vocabulary, approved accelerated students write the terms but may omit copying definitions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maintaining the accelerated path:&lt;/strong&gt; Independently earn at least 90% on each Notebook, Checkpoint, quiz, and unit assessment. A score of 80–89% returns you to the standard path without intervention solely for falling below 90%. A score below 80% also requires TOR intervention. Eligibility is considered separately for each unit.&lt;/p&gt;</intro>
